# Rules live on my-dashboard only

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard agent work.

## When updating `.cursor/rules/` for the live board

- Canonical rules live in **`/Users/diana/my-dashboard/.cursor/rules/`**
- **Commit and push** those rule files to **`dianacodesit/my-dashboard`** (remote `my-dashboard`)
- **Never** commit or push dashboard rule mirrors to **`dianacodesit/task-dashboard`**

## Never

- “Rule mirrors only” commits on task-dashboard
- Pushing overview / packing / chrome rule updates to task-dashboard `main`
- Treating task-dashboard as the rules repo for the live board

## Always

1. Edit rules under `/Users/diana/my-dashboard/.cursor/rules/`
2. If the workspace is task-dashboard, still write the rule into **my-dashboard** and commit/push **there**
3. Keep product HTML (`everything.html`, etc.) on my-dashboard — same destination
